  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: $f(x)=\\int_0^{x^2} \\frac{t^2-5 t+4}{2+e^t} d t$...(1)\nto find extremum points we solve $f^{\\prime}(x)=0$\nso differentiating equation (i) using Newton Leibnitz Rule,\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{\\left(x^2-1\\right)\\left(x^2-4\\right)}{2+e^{x^2}} \\cdot(2 x) \\quad \\text { so, } f^{\\prime}(x)=0 \\text { at } x=0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2$",
    "image": null
  },
